<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siyannu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siyannu was a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> kingdom on the Syrian coast south of Ugarit, around modern Tell Siyannu near Jableh. Long a dependency of Ugarit, it was detached from Ugaritic control by the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-ii">Mursili II</a> in the late fourteenth century BCE and placed under the authority of the Hittite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> at Carchemish, reducing Ugarit's territory.</p></div>
